// n28 — a bounded string constant longer than its own bound.
//
// `string<3>` is three characters and the value is four. The check is on the
// character count, not on the byte count, which is the same choice the wide
// forms make.
//
// omniidl 4.3.4, measured 2026-08-25:
//   Length of bounded string constant exceeds bound
//
// **The second shape sharing `const-value-range` with n20's out-of-range
// integer** (n27 is the first). The hint keyed there offers *"widen the
// type — `short` to `long`, `long` to `long long`, or the signed form to the
// unsigned one"*, none of which is an edit for a string: the answer is to widen
// the *bound* or shorten the value, which is what the message already says and
// the hint contradicts by omission.
//
// 경계 있는 문자열 상수는 자기 경계를 넘을 수 없다. 정수 범위 초과와 같은 규칙에
// 접수되므로, 정수를 보고 쓰인 힌트가 붙는다.
module n28 {
  const string<3> TAG = "abcd";
};
